Algorithm L (Lookup).
Given v - real number, intensity, v finite, v not NaN,
      R - fixed sequence of n characters, ordered dark to light,
      n - length of R, n >= 1,
find  r_k - character at position k in R,
      where k is the integer in [0, n-1] nearest to v * (n-1).

Model:      sequential
Terminates: yes

[Compute + Decide] L1. [Clamp.]  call C(v, 0, 1) -> v'.           (v' ∈ [0,1].)        -> L2
[Compute]          L2. [Scale.]  set k <- round(v' * (n-1)).      (k nearest index.)    -> L3
[Compute]          L3. [Guard.]  set k <- min(k, n-1).            (k ∈ [0, n-1].)       -> L4
[Halt]             L4. [Return.] output R[k].                     (r_k is correct.)     -> done  ■

verify
termination:  4 fixed steps, no loop
correctness:  R[k] exists and k ∈ [0, n-1] holds after L3
invariant:    v' ∈ [0,1] at L2 · k nearest index at L3